{"demo_id": "00049_2110_02861.txt::sent::66", "doc_id": "00049_2110_02861.txt", "context_type": "sentence", "sent_idx": 95, "context_text": "We report on benchmarks in neural machine translation (Ott et al., 2018) 2 trained on WMT'16 (Sennrich et al., 2016) and evaluated on en-de WMT'14 (Macháček and Bojar, 2014), large-scale language modeling (Lewis et al., 2021; Brown et al., 2020) and RoBERTa pretraining (Liu et al., 2019) on English CC-100 + RoBERTa corpus (Nagel, 2016; Gokaslan and Cohen, 2019; Zhu et al., 2015; Wenzek et al., 2020), finetuning the pretrained masked language model RoBERTa (Liu et al., 2019) 3 on GLUE (Wang et al., 2018a), ResNet-50 v1.5 image classification (He et al., 2016) 4 on ImageNet-1k (Deng et al., 2009), and Moco v2 contrastive image pretraining and linear finetuning (Chen et al., 2020b) 5 on ImageNet-1k (Deng et al., 2009).", "entities": [{"text": "neural machine translation", "start_token": 2511, "end_token": 2513, "start_char": 14013, "end_char": 14039, "ner_label": "Task"}, {"text": "WMT'16", "start_token": 2525, "end_token": 2525, "start_char": 14072, "end_char": 14078, "ner_label": "Dataset"}, {"text": "en-de WMT'14", "start_token": 2537, "end_token": 2540, "start_char": 14120, "end_char": 14132, "ner_label": "Dataset"}, {"text": "large-scale language modeling", "start_token": 2549, "end_token": 2553, "start_char": 14161, "end_char": 14190, "ner_label": "Method"}, {"text": "RoBERTa pretraining", "start_token": 2570, "end_token": 2571, "start_char": 14236, "end_char": 14255, "ner_label": "Method"}, {"text": "English CC-100", "start_token": 2581, "end_token": 2582, "start_char": 14278, "end_char": 14292, "ner_label": "Dataset"}, {"text": "RoBERTa", "start_token": 2584, "end_token": 2584, "start_char": 14295, "end_char": 14302, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "finetuning", "start_token": 2612, "end_token": 2612, "start_char": 14390, "end_char": 14400, "ner_label": "Method"}, {"text": "pretrained masked language model", "start_token": 2614, "end_token": 2617, "start_char": 14405, "end_char": 14437, "ner_label": "ModelArchitecture"}, {"text": "RoBERTa", "start_token": 2618, "end_token": 2618, "start_char": 14438, "end_char": 14445, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "GLUE", "start_token": 2629, "end_token": 2629, "start_char": 14470, "end_char": 14474, "ner_label": "Dataset"}, {"text": "ResNet-50 v1.5", "start_token": 2639, "end_token": 2640, "start_char": 14497, "end_char": 14511, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "image classification", "start_token": 2641, "end_token": 2642, "start_char": 14512, "end_char": 14532, "ner_label": "Task"}, {"text": "ImageNet-1k", "start_token": 2653, "end_token": 2653, "start_char": 14556, "end_char": 14567, "ner_label": "Dataset"}, {"text": "Moco v2", "start_token": 2664, "end_token": 2665, "start_char": 14593, "end_char": 14600, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "contrastive image pretraining", "start_token": 2666, "end_token": 2668, "start_char": 14601, "end_char": 14630, "ner_label": "Method"}, {"text": "linear finetuning", "start_token": 2670, "end_token": 2671, "start_char": 14635, "end_char": 14652, "ner_label": "Method"}, {"text": "ImageNet-1k", "start_token": 2682, "end_token": 2682, "start_char": 14679, "end_char": 14690, "ner_label": "Dataset"}], "labels_present": ["Dataset", "MLModel", "Method", "ModelArchitecture", "Task"]}
{"demo_id": "10003_2105_14444.txt::sent::92", "doc_id": "10003_2105_14444.txt", "context_type": "sentence", "sent_idx": 111, "context_text": "We compare our NAS-BERT models with hand-designed BERT models under the same parameter size and latency (denoted as BERT 60, BERT 30, BERT 10 and BERT 5 We mainly compare our NAS-BERT with methods whose teacher model is BERT base for a fair comparison including 1) DistilBERT [37], which uses knowledge distillation on the pre-training stage; 2) BERT-PKD [41], which distills the knowledge from the intermediate layers and the final output logits on the pre-training stage; 3) BERT-of-Theseus [53], which uses module replacement for compression; 4) MiniLM [49], which transfers the knowledge from the self-attention module; 5) PD-BERT [44], which distills the knowledge from the target domain in BERT training; 6) DynaBERT [16], which uses network rewiring to adjust width and depth of BERT for each downstream task.", "entities": [{"text": "NAS-BERT", "start_token": 3977, "end_token": 3979, "start_char": 20580, "end_char": 20588, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT", "start_token": 3985, "end_token": 3985, "start_char": 20615, "end_char": 20619, "ner_label": "ModelArchitecture"}, {"text": "BERT 60", "start_token": 3997, "end_token": 3998, "start_char": 20681, "end_char": 20688, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT 30", "start_token": 4000, "end_token": 4001, "start_char": 20691, "end_char": 20698, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT 10", "start_token": 4003, "end_token": 4004, "start_char": 20701, "end_char": 20708, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT 5", "start_token": 4006, "end_token": 4007, "start_char": 20713, "end_char": 20719, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "NAS-BERT", "start_token": 4012, "end_token": 4014, "start_char": 20742, "end_char": 20750, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "BERT base", "start_token": 4021, "end_token": 4022, "start_char": 20787, "end_char": 20796, "ner_label": "ModelArchitecture"}, {"text