{"demo_id": "00012_2102_07033.txt::sent::30", "doc_id": "00012_2102_07033.txt", "context_type": "sentence", "sent_idx": 38, "context_text": "In summary, we make the following contribu-tions: i) introduce PAQ, 65 M QA-pairs automatically generated from Wikipedia, and demonstrate the importance of global filtering for high quality ii) introduce RePAQ, a QA system designed to utilize PAQ and demonstrate how it can be optimised for memory, speed or accuracy iii) investigate the utility of PAQ for CBQA models, improving by 5% but note significant headroom to RePAQ iv) demonstrate RePAQ's strength on selective QA, enabling us to combine RePAQ with a state-of-the-art QA model, making it both more accurate and 2x faster 1 2 Open-Domain Question Answering ODQA is the task of answering natural language factoid question from an open set of domains.", "entities": [{"text": "PAQ", "start_token": 1269, "end_token": 1269, "start_char": 6255, "end_char": 6258, "ner_label": "Dataset"}, {"text": "Wikipedia", "start_token": 1279, "end_token": 1279, "start_char": 6302, "end_char": 6311, "ner_label": "DataSource"}, {"text": "global filtering", "start_token": 1286, "end_token": 1287, "start_char": 6347, "end_char": 6363, "ner_label": "Method"}, {"text": "RePAQ", "start_token": 1294, "end_token": 1294, "start_char": 6395, "end_char": 6400, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "QA", "start_token": 1297, "end_token": 1297, "start_char": 6404, "end_char": 6406, "ner_label": "Task"}, {"text": "PAQ", "start_token": 1302, "end_token": 1302, "start_char": 6434, "end_char": 6437, "ner_label": "Dataset"}, {"text": "PAQ", "start_token": 1322, "end_token": 1322, "start_char": 6540, "end_char": 6543, "ner_label": "Dataset"}, {"text": "CBQA", "start_token": 1324, "end_token": 1324, "start_char": 6548, "end_char": 6552, "ner_label": "Task"}, {"text": "RePAQ", "start_token": 1336, "end_token": 1336, "start_char": 6610, "end_char": 6615, "ner_label": "MLModel"}, {"text": "RePAQ's", "start_token": 1340, "end